OVERVIEW: Start a server, or a whole project.

USAGE: portly start [<server>] [--project <project>] [--json] [--api-port <api-port>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <server>                Server name or id. Use "project/server" to
                          disambiguate.

OPTIONS:
  --project <project>     Act on every server in this project instead.
  --json                  Print raw JSON instead of a human summary.
  --api-port <api-port>   Override the control API port.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

---
OVERVIEW: Register a project folder.

USAGE: portly add-project --name <name> --path <path> [--icon <icon>] [--color <color>] [--memory-limit <memory-limit>] [--json] [--api-port <api-port>]

OPTIONS:
  --name <name>           Project name.
  --path <path>           Absolute path to the project folder.
  --icon <icon>           SF Symbol name shown in the sidebar, for example
                          globe.
  --color <color>         Hex color for the project icon.
  --memory-limit <memory-limit>
                          Project memory policy: inherit, off, or a size such
                          as 5GB.
  --json                  Print raw JSON instead of a human summary.
  --api-port <api-port>   Override the control API port.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

---
OVERVIEW: Add a server to a project.

USAGE: portly add-server [<options>] --project <project> --name <name> --command <command>

OPTIONS:
  --project <project>     Project name or id.
  --name <name>           Server name, for example "web".
  --command <command>     Command to run, executed through a login shell.
  --port <port>           Port the server listens on.
  --directory <directory> Working directory, relative to the project folder or
                          absolute.
  --health-url <health-url>
                          Health check path or URL, for example /api/health.
  --env <env>             Environment variables as KEY=VALUE.
  --action <action>       Maintenance actions as NAME=COMMAND.
  --auto-restart/--no-auto-restart
                          Restart automatically after a crash. (default:
                          --auto-restart)
  --idle-timeout <idle-timeout>
                          Stop after this long without output or CPU activity:
                          a duration such as 30m, off, or inherit (default).
  --start                 Start the server right after adding it.
  --json                  Print raw JSON instead of a human summary.
  --api-port <api-port>   Override the control API port.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

